# ttychatter C changelog

## 0.6.1-c-cli

### Changed
- Moved default C storage into the shared OpenRouter ttychatter namespace:
  ~/.config/ttychatter/openrouter/config,
  ~/.config/ttychatter/openrouter/api-key.gpg,
  ~/.config/ttychatter/openrouter/model-favorites,
  ~/.cache/ttychatter/openrouter/models.json,
  ~/.local/share/ttychatter/openrouter/sessions, and
  ~/.local/share/ttychatter/openrouter/attachments.
- Preserved legacy C config/key compatibility by reading ~/.config/ttychatter/config
  and ~/.config/ttychatter/api-key.gpg as fallbacks when the new OpenRouter
  files are absent.
- Added config aliases API_KEY, HISTORY_LIMIT, and MODEL_FILTER_CHAT_COMPLETIONS
  for better cross-client config compatibility.
- Changed new C session writes to the shared line-oriented transcript format
  used by the OpenRouter ttychatter clients.
- Kept the 0.6.0 C marker-block session format readable as a legacy format.
- Resolved --interactive SESSION through the same named-session rules as
  --resume, --show-memory, and --rename-session.
- Fixed `make check` so it builds the ttychatter binary before running
  version/help smoke checks.
- Changed startup notice output so new logs begin with the exact pre-chat line
  requested by the project owner, and --interactive prints that line before the
  prompt.

### Documented
- Clarified the two address modes: explicit file-in/file-out paths versus
  named sessions under SESSION_DIR.
- Corrected FILES, CONFIGURATION, SESSION FORMAT, README, WALKTHROUGH, and
  changelog text to remove the old storage discrepancy.

## 0.6.0-c-cli

### Added
- `--routers` shorthand for `--models --model-type routers`
- `--allow-missing-tokens` model-listing flag
- `--unbookmark-model MODEL` alias for `--unfavorite-model MODEL`
- `--resume SESSION` interactive-session shorthand
- `--save` support for successful `--test-model MODEL`
- Interactive `:list` command
- Interactive `:rename NAME` command
- Interactive `:select-model` command
- Interactive `:edit-memory` command
- Interactive `:pending` alias for `:attachments`
- Interactive `:unbookmark MODEL` alias for `:unfavorite MODEL`

### Changed
- `--loopback-file` now appends responses instead of overwriting the file
- Interactive mode now more closely matches the Bash/Python colon-command vocabulary
- Help output documents the new router, resume, save, and missing-token controls

### Notes
- This pass focuses on parity with ttychatter.python runtime commands and command-line flags, not on ncurses UI mechanics.
- The C client remains a traditional Unix file-in/file-out client with an optional line-oriented REPL.

## 0.5.0-c-cli

### Added
- Additional feature-parity work against ttychatter.python reference behavior
- Config support for MODEL_TEST_PROMPT
- Config support for SEND_INPUT as a cross-client parity key
- Config support for EDITOR
- Config support for DEMO_MODE
- Config support for MODEL_TYPE_FILTER
- Config support for MODEL_FILTER_GENERATE_CONTENT
- Config support for MODEL_FILTER_REQUIRE_TOKENS
- Config support for MODEL_FILTER_HIDE_PREVIEW
- Config support for MODEL_MIN_INPUT_TOKENS
- Config support for MODEL_MIN_OUTPUT_TOKENS
- `--list` session listing command
- `--rename-session OLD NEW` command
- `--show-memory SESSION` command
- `--clear-memory SESSION` command
- `--edit-memory SESSION` command
- `--editor-prompt [SESSION]` command
- `--credits` command
- `--search-sessions TEXT` command
- `--select-model` numbered cached model selector
- `--min-input-tokens N`
- `--min-output-tokens N`
- `--hide-preview`
- `--show-preview`
- `--require-tokens`
- `--send-input VALUE`
- `--theme VALUE`
- `--code-attachment-min-lines N`
- Interactive `:clear-memory` command
- Explicit context snapshot markers for edited memory
- Memory-clear marker handling in context reconstruction

### Changed
- `--help` now documents the expanded command set
- `--config` now prints more cross-client parity keys
- `--test-model` now uses MODEL_TEST_PROMPT from config
- Model listing now honors more filter settings from config and flags
- `--all` disables model filters for model listing
- Session memory parsing now honors explicit memory-clear markers and context snapshots

### Notes
- Some keys such as SEND_INPUT and THEME are accepted for config compatibility even though the file-in/file-out C client has no ncurses input field or visual theme.
- The C client remains command-line/file-oriented; ncurses-only UI mechanics are represented by command-line equivalents.

## 0.4.0-c-cli

### Added
- Interactive mode with colon commands
- `--interactive` / `-i`
- Runtime commands such as `:help`, `:models`, `:attach`, `:editor`, `:doctor`, and `:quit`

## 0.3.0-c-cli

### Added
- Confirm-live-send support
- Startup notice support
- Loopback default config support
- Model sorting and favorites-only listing

## 0.2.0-c-cli

### Added
- Demo mode
- Model favorites
- Config set/unset
- Session search

## 0.1.0-c-cli

### Initial release
- File-in/file-out OpenRouter command-line client
- API-key setup including GPG support
- Model list/update/test basics
- Session log append/resume
- Attachments and code-block extraction basics
